From 233fed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JordiPosthumus <jordiposthumus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 02:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] STQ1_0 Metal kernels: decode four-block charfull + y-column hoist
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds full Metal support for Tencent Hy4-preview's STQ1_0 quant (3:4-sparse
symmetric ternary, 42B/256 weights) — the AngelSlim patch ships CPU/CUDA only.

- kernel_mul_mv_stq1_0_f32 (decode): group-aligned float4 loads, compact
  char4 vector codebook, 8 lanes/block with four blocks in flight per SIMD
  group; y-columns hoisted out of the row loop and a split accumulator.
  ~2.1x over the first working element-offset mapping; ~4-5% further from
  the hoist at the 6144xN expert shape. 42B stride => 2-byte-aligned ushort
  qs loads only (uint loads are misaligned on odd blocks).
- kernel_mul_mv_ext_stq1_0_f32_r1_2..5 (small batch), kernel_mul_mm_stq1_0_f32/_f16
  (prefill, simdgroup_half8x8), kernel_mul_mm_id (routed experts),
  kernel_mul_mv_id (MoE decode), kernel_get_rows_stq1_0, kernel_cpy_stq1_0_*.
- host plumbing: pipeline cases in ggml-metal-device.cpp, mul_mv_ext admission
  in ggml-metal-ops.cpp.

Apply on top of AngelSlim 0001-hyv4-architecture.patch + 0002-stq1_0-quant.patch.
Validated on M3 Ultra: Metal vs float reference max_abs_err 0.0000/0.0001/0.0232
at BS 1/8/32.
